DESCRIPTION Returns one deduped first-touch Exposure row per Entity in one Run, shaped as the Stats Engine's DedupeExposureRow.

# `experiment_id` is deliberately absent: DedupeExposureRowSchema is strict, so any
# column not on it fails the parse in the Analysis Worker. The Run pins the
# Experiment, and serve_deduped_exposures already filters on both.
#
# `__multiple__` rows are deliberately NOT filtered here. The quarantine rule keeps
# them out of the analysis arms, but the Stats Engine applies that itself
# (packages/stats/src/exposure-denominator.ts) and counts the same rows into
# health.multiple_count / multiple_rate. Dropping them in SQL would report zero
# variant conflicts for a Run that had them -- silencing the exact defect the
# quarantine exists to surface.

NODE stats_input_rows
SQL >
    SELECT
        app_id,
        environment_id,
        id_type,
        run_id,
        targeting_key_hash,
        variant,
        first_exposure_ts,
        -- The ungated anchor. The Activation gate re-anchors window_anchor to the
        -- Entity's activation_ts, but that gate is per-Run configuration held in D1
        -- (runs.activation_metric_id) which the Analysis Worker cannot read, so no
        -- Run is gated end to end yet. Emitted explicitly rather than omitted: the
        -- consumer would otherwise substitute first_exposure_ts for a missing
        -- column, which reads as a computed anchor and is not one.
        first_exposure_ts AS window_anchor
    FROM serve_deduped_exposures
    ORDER BY variant, targeting_key_hash

TYPE ENDPOINT
